Provide a stdckdint.h fallback for toolchains whose C library does not ship the
C23 checked-integer header (clang 15 / OHOS 6.0 sysroot).

zathura 2026.07.18 includes <stdckdint.h> and calls ckd_mul() in
zathura/types.c.  The OHOS SDK is clang 15, which predates the finalised C23
header, so the include fails with "'stdckdint.h' file not found".  Map the
checked multiplication onto the compiler builtin, which has been available in
clang for far longer and implements exactly the semantics the C23 macro
requires: the result is the wrapped value on overflow and the call returns true
when the operation overflowed.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [portability shim for an older toolchain]
--- a/zathura/types.c	2026-09-30 01:46:10.847782413 +0800
+++ b/zathura/types.c	2026-09-30 01:46:11.082452104 +0800
@@ -3,7 +3,23 @@
 #include "types.h"
 
 #include <stdlib.h>
-#include <stdckdint.h>
+#if defined(__has_include)
+#  if __has_include(<stdckdint.h>)
+#    include <stdckdint.h>
+#  else
+#    define ZATHURA_NEEDS_STDCKDINT_FALLBACK 1
+#  endif
+#elif defined(__STDC_VERSION__) && __STDC_VERSION__ >= 202311L
+#  include <stdckdint.h>
+#else
+#  define ZATHURA_NEEDS_STDCKDINT_FALLBACK 1
+#endif
+
+#ifdef ZATHURA_NEEDS_STDCKDINT_FALLBACK
+/* C23 <stdckdint.h> is not provided by this toolchain (clang 15 / OHOS).
+ * Reimplement the subset zathura uses on top of the compiler builtins. */
+#  define ckd_mul(result, a, b) __builtin_mul_overflow((a), (b), (result))
+#endif
 #include <girara/datastructures.h>
 #include <glib.h>
 
